.th PALS IV
.sh NAME
pals - PALS local terminal interface
.sh DESCRIPTION
Local terminals connected via the PALS interface
behave as described in tty(IV).

Device numbers 0/0, 0/1, 0/2 ... correspond to addresses x'10', x'12', x'14'
etc.
Available baud rates and corresponding PALS 'command 2'
values (see boot(VIII)) are:

.nf
.in +8
.ul 1
baud    cmd2
300      38
1200     78
2400     B8
4800     F8
.in -8
.sh FILES
/dev/tty?
.sh "SEE ALSO"
tty(IV), stty(I), ttys(V), init(VIII)
